{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"curl -L --silent http://pepquery.org/document.html -o /tmp/pepdoc.html && wc -c /tmp/pepdoc.html && grep -n -- '-db\\\\|-fixMod\\\\|-varMod\\\\|-tol\\\\|-ms\\\\|-minCharge\\\\|-maxCharge\\\\|-fast\\\\|-enzyme\\\\|-missed\\\\|-frag' /tmp/pepdoc.html | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"57380 /tmp/pepdoc.html\n224:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-ms</b>: MS/MS data used for identification. <a href=\"http://www.matrixscience.com/help/data_file_help.html#GEN\">MGF</a>, <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC3013463/\">mzML</a>, <a href=\"http://tools.proteomecenter.org/wiki/index.php?title=Formats:mzXML\">mzXML</a>, mgf.gz, mzML.gz, mzXML.gz and Thermo raw formats are supported. </li>\n249:      <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-db</b>: A protein reference database in FASTA format. For example, a protein sequence database from <a href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/refseq/\">RefSeq</a>, <a href=\"https://www.gencodegenes.org/\">GENCODE</a>, <a href=\"http://www.ensembl.org/index.html\">Ensembl</a> or <a href=\"https://www.uniprot.org/\">UniProt</a>. A string like\n265:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-tol</b>: Precursor ion m/z tolerance, default is 10.</li>\n266:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-tolu</b>: The unit of precursor ion m/z tolerance, default is ppm.</li>\n268:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-fixMod</b>: Fixed modification, the format is like : 1,2,3. Use '-printPTM' to show all\n270:                         there is no fixed modification, set it as '-fixMod no' or '-fixMod 0'.</li>\n271:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-varMod</b>: Variable modification, the format is same with -fixMod. Default is 2\n273:                         '-varMod no' or '-varMod 0'.</li>\n286:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-fast</b>: Choose to use the fast mode for searching or not. In fast mode, only one better match from reference peptide-based competitive filtering steps will be returned. A peptide identified or not is not affected by this setting. For most applications, add '-fast' will speed up the analysis.</li>\n292:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-minCharge</b>: The minimum charge to consider if the charge state is not available, default is 2.</li>\n293:\t  <li class=\"divcsstutorialli\"><b>-maxCharge</b>: The maximum charge to consider if the charge state is not available, default is 3.</li>\n394:            <td>The delta score between the match to the target peptide and the \"best match\" from competitive filtering based on reference sequences (<a href=\"https://genome.cshlp.org/content/29/3/485/F2.expansion.html\" target=\"_blank\">step 3</a>). In fast model when '-fast' is set, the \"best match\" may not be real best match.</td>\n398:            <td>The delta score between the match to the target peptide and the \"best match\" from competitive filtering based on unrestricted post-translational modification searching. (<a href=\"https://genome.cshlp.org/content/29/3/485/F2.expansion.html\" target=\"_blank\">step 5</a>). In fast model when '-fast' is set, the \"best match\" may not be real best match..</td>\n604:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_LUAD_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000153,CPTAC_PDA_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000270,CPTAC_UCEC_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000125 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n612:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_LUAD_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000153 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n627:\t  <pre>-fixMod 1 -&gt; Fixed modification: 1 = Carbamidomethylation of C\n628:-varMod 2 -&gt; Variable modification: 2 = Oxidation of M\n629:-tol -&gt; Precursor mass tolerance: 10.0 ppm\n637:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -db iPRG2015/iPRG2015_no6.fasta -ms iPRG2015/JD_06232014_sample1-A.mgf -fixMod 1 -varMod 2 -tol 10 -itol 0.05 -i LLSYVDDEAFIRDVAK,VGDANPALQK -o out</pre>\n643:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_LUAD_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000153,CPTAC_PDA_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000270,CPTAC_UCEC_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000125 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n645:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b all -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n647:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n649:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b p -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n651:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b w -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n653:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b g -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n655:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b a -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n657:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b u -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_kras_g12d/ -i LVVVGADGVGK</pre>\n659:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_TCGA_Colon_Cancer_Proteome_PDC000111 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_out/ -i LVVVGADGVGK,NPLLDLAAYDQEGR</pre>\n661:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_TCGA_Colon_Cancer_Proteome_PDC000111 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_out/ -i pep.txt</pre>\n665:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_LUAD_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000153 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_out/ -i AHSSMVGVNLPQK -s 2</pre>\n667:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_LUAD_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000153 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_out/ -i psm.txt -s 2</pre>\n671:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_TCGA_Colon_Cancer_Proteome_PDC000111 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_out/ -i MKKFFDSRREQGGSGLGSGSSGGGGSTSGLGSGYIGRVFGIGRQQVTVDEVLAEGGFAIVFLVRTSNGMKCALKRMFVNNEHDLQVCKREIQIMRDLSGHKNIVGYIDSSINNVSSGDVWEVLILMDFCRGGQVVNLMNQRLQTGFTENEVLQIFCDTCEAVARLHQCKTPIIHRDLKVENILLHDRKVFHELTQTDKMGAQELLR -t protein</pre>\n673:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_TCGA_Colon_Cancer_Proteome_PDC000111 -db gencode:human -hc -o pepquery_out/ -i  -t DNA</pre>\n675:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -b CPTAC_LUAD_Discovery_Study_Proteome_PDC000153 -db swissprot:human -hc -o pepquery_out/ -i \"sp|P07205|PGK2_HUMAN\" -t protein -s 2</pre>\n686:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -varMod 2 -fixMod 0 -t protein -s 2 -ti 0,1 -tol 50 -itol 0.05 -hc -db uniprot-proteome_UP000005640_format.fasta -i F2Z2R5,F6T542,K7EMC0,K7EMY3,K7ESA5,Q8TDI0 -b \"MSV000088555:j11456.mzML|b10335.mzML\" -o pepquery_out/HDAC1/CHD5</pre>\n725:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -i VLHPLEGAVVIIFK -ms \"mzspec:PXD000561:Adult_Frontalcortex_bRP_Elite_85_f09:scan:17555\" -db swissprot:human -hc -s 2 -o usi -itol 0.05</pre>\n728:\t  <pre>java -jar pepquery-2.0.2/pepquery-2.0.2.jar -ms \"mzspec:PXD010154:01284_E04_P013188_B00_N29_R1.mzML:scan:31291\" -i DQNGTWEMESNENFEGYMK -itol 0.05 -hc -db swissprot:human -o usi -s 2 -varMod 2 -fixMod  1 -tol 10 -ti 0,1</pre>\n748:\t\t<p class=\"divcss5\">Once we have the MS/MS data indexed, we can give the folder (this is the folder for parameter -o when we build MS/MS index) which containing the indexed MS/MS files to parameter -ms when we do PepQuery search. The orginal MS/MS data is not required any more for PepQuery search after we have the indexed MS/MS files.</p>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
